name c01m08-black-mariah
timeout 900
time 1996-03-24T20:00:00Z

# F-22 LIGHTNING II (NovaLogic 1996), CAMPAIGN ONE, SORTIE 1.8 OF 8 — "BLACK MARIAH". THE LAST.
# Spec: mods/f22/doc/campaign.md 2. Geometry: mods/f22/doc/terrain.md 3. Substitutions:
# mods/f22/doc/substitutions.md. The five campaign-wide disclosures: c01m01-snake-eyes.fbm.
#
# THE TASK [ORF, verbatim]: "Final bombing of Chang Tzu Mings base in Laotian territory. [...] This
# mission will be flown under the cover of night." Storm Squadron sweeps ahead of Vampire Squadron's
# B-1B onto Objective Talbot, briefed 85 NM N; measured 87.0 NM on bearing 17.6 deg [ORF].
#
# THIS IS THE FAR TALBOT (campaign.md 6). Sortie 1.2's Talbot is an assembly house 88.3 km away from
# this one. One codename, two places, kept as found.
#
# SUBSTITUTIONS IN THIS FILE
#   B-1B Lancer (Vampire Squadron) -> `f16` x 2 with `mk84`, AND THIS IS THE CAMPAIGN'S LARGEST
#     SUBSTITUTION. The catalogue's only heavy bomber is `tu95`, and `tu95` is a MOVER: `Stations` 0,
#     no fire control, NOTHING IT CAN DROP. A mover cannot bomb, and `set task attack` exists only on
#     the F-16 and MiG-29 modules — no catalogue row has an air-to-ground phase at all. So the choice
#     is between a bomber that cannot bomb and a fighter-bomber that can, and the mission's whole
#     subject is whether SOMEBODY ELSE'S aircraft completes a bomb run. The direction of the error is
#     enormous and runs both ways: two Mk-84 instead of 84 Mk-82; a 9 g airframe that can defend
#     itself instead of a bomber that cannot; and no B-1B signature, altitude profile or speed.
#   Chang's command centre -> `target_soft`. The .ORF loads `RBA_H` here and `RBB_H` for sortie 1.2's
#     assembly house — the same suffix, so the same object class, so the same fragility class. That is
#     an argument from the data and not from convenience; no source gives hardening for anything in
#     this campaign, and the one object this campaign treats as structure (the bridge of 1.3) has a
#     different model family (`CTR`/`CTRMP`) and is declared `target_hard` there.
#   EF2000 -> `f15c`; MiG-29 -> `mig29`; MiG-27 -> `mig23`. As in 1.7 and 1.1.
#   SA-2 -> `sa2`. EXACT.
#   SA-9 Gaskin -> `sa18` (9K38 Igla). The SA-9 is a vehicle with four INFRARED, ALL-ASPECT rounds and
#     a 2.6 kg warhead [MAN p.86-97*]. The catalogue has no vehicle-mounted IR SAM; `sa18` is the row
#     whose GUIDANCE PRINCIPLE matches — infrared, all-aspect (OpticalAzHalfDeg 180), flare-defeatable,
#     5.2 km reach, 3 500 m ceiling. What is wrong: it is a shoulder launcher, so it does not move, it
#     carries two rounds and not four, and `core/FBSite.h` says outright that the Igla's documented
#     flare resistance is not modelled. `sa8` was the alternative and was refused: it is a vehicle, but
#     it is RADAR-command-guided, and guidance is what decides an engagement.
#
# THE SWEEP IS REQUIRED TO KILL NOTHING, WHICH IS WHY ITS KILLS ARE ON THE SWEEP AND THE VERDICT IS
# NOT. campaign.md: "the verdict hangs entirely on someone else's aircraft, which makes this the
# campaign's only true escort-of-strike test." The three interceptors have to be covered by somebody
# or their deaths end the run CRASH/exit 2, so `s8swp1`/`s8swp2` carry the `kill` lines — and the
# sortie's verdict is `s8vam1`'s UNIT_RESULT, which contains no kill at all.
#
# NIGHT, 0300 local at the equinox. `mission CLOCK` at t = 0 logs the computed sun elevation and is
# the check. The ZU-23 class of gun is absent for the reason given in 1.7: the visual channel reads
# zero at night, so an optically laid gun here would be a unit that cannot act.
#
# READING RULE (binding). The verdict is `s8vam1`'s UNIT_RESULT, and campaign.md's condition is BOTH
# halves of it.
#   SUCCESS/exit 0 = `s8cmd` destroyed AND Vampire lead combat-effective at the end.
#   `s8vam1` FAIL = Vampire was shot: the sweep failed at its only job, whatever it killed.
#   `s8vam1` TIMEOUT with `kill unit s8cmd` unmet while Vampire lives = the strike did not reach or the
#   weapon did not, which is c01m03's measurement and not this file's.
#   THE SWEEP'S OWN RESULT IS NOT THE SORTIE'S under any outcome. A sweep that is wiped out while
#   Vampire delivers and comes home has flown this sortie successfully, and the exit code will say
#   FAIL. That is the sharpest case in the campaign of "the exit code is not the verdict".

# MEASURED (exit 3, real ground): THE SWEEP EATS THE MAGAZINE AND SURVIVES IT — AND THE STRIKE THEN
# MISSES ON THE CCRP PLANE.
#   t = 0.0 s           `mission CLOCK sunElDeg=-46.091` — night
#   t = 123.2-166.5 s   `s8sa2` fires all six v-750 at the SWEEP at the SAME six timestamps as over the
#                       flat plane. ALL SIX MISS. Over the plane round five killed `s8swp1` at
#                       t = 182.6 with 9.42 m and ended the run there
#   t = 386.6 s         Vampire releases, `planeM = 511.926` — the ground under the RELEASE POINT
#   t = 409.0 / 409.1 s both mk84 impact 20.2085 N / 100.812 E, ~215 m SHORT of the command centre.
#                       `s8cmd` INTACT
#   verdict             all three of Storm/Vampire TIMEOUT, `kill unit s8cmd` unmet, exit 3
#
# AND THE ENGINE FINDING REAL GROUND ADDED, measured here for the first time because a flat plane
# cannot show it: THE CCRP IMPACT PLANE IS THE RELEASE POINT'S GROUND ELEVATION, NOT THE TARGET'S.
# `FBF16Module.cpp` hands `SetSteerpoint(swp->Lat, swp->Lon, GroundAslM)` — this tick's sample under
# the AIRCRAFT — and `FBF16FireControl::SolveGroundAttack` solves the ballistic integration against it.
# Here: release ground 511.9 m, target ground 834.4 m, plane error +322.5 m, and the bomb is therefore
# released 215 m too early on the ground track and clips the up-slope at 778.8 m. The computer's own
# `aimMissM` reported 65.3 m and it was 215 m out. Over a 0 m plane the two elevations are equal by
# construction and the error is exactly zero, which is why nothing had ever seen it.
# It is a NAMED limitation in the code's own comment, not a regression — but it is now a measured one.
#
# AND THE ENGINE FINDING THIS SORTIE EXISTS TO PRODUCE, stated as a limit and not as a bug report:
#   A PACKAGE MISSION CANNOT MEASURE ITS OWN SUBJECT IF ANY MEMBER DIES FIRST. The run ends at the
#   first decisive failure and at the first physical K.O. (doc/missions/verdict.md, the combination
#   rule), so the escort doing exactly its job — absorbing an S-75 battalion's whole magazine at
#   t = 123-167 — terminates the run 210 s before the strike it was protecting would have released.
#   No declaration available today avoids it: covering the sweep's loss with a hostile `kill`
#   objective removes the DECISIVE failure but not the physical K.O. that follows it, and no lateral
#   offset inside this box puts a 5 000 m sweep outside the S-75's 30 km slant reach.
#   THE CONSEQUENCE FOR THIS TITLE: campaign.md 3 calls 1.8 "the campaign's only true escort-of-strike
#   test". It cannot be run as one until a mission can declare that the run continues past a friendly
#   loss. That is the sortie's actual deliverable.

unit s8swp1
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight storm8 1
  spawn 19.61106 100.61071 5000 17.6 480      # 70 km short of Talbot, ahead of and above Vampire
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 1 aim9
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set store 8 aim120
  set store 9 aim9
  set gun_rounds 480
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 20.72420 100.98689 5000 480              # 60 km beyond Talbot: the sweep goes THROUGH, not to
  objective kill unit s8ef
  objective kill unit s8ful
  objective protect unit s8vam1
  objective survive

unit s8swp2
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight storm8 2
  spawn 19.60699 100.62435 5000 17.6 480      # 1.5 km across track from the sweep lead
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 1 aim9
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set store 8 aim120
  set store 9 aim9
  set gun_rounds 480
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 20.72420 100.98689 5000 480
  objective kill unit s8flg
  objective protect unit s8vam2
  objective survive

unit s8vam1
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight vamp8 1
  spawn 19.39699 100.53868 3000 17.6 450      # 95 km short of Talbot, 25 km behind the sweep
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off                            # a bomber does not radiate
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set gun_rounds 480
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 20.21044 100.81294 3000 450              # THE AIM POINT: Chang's command centre
  wp 20.33888 100.85637 3000 450              # egress 15 km beyond
  objective kill unit s8cmd
  objective survive

unit s8vam2
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight vamp8 2
  spawn 19.39292 100.55229 3000 17.6 450      # 1.5 km across track from Vampire lead
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set gun_rounds 480
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 20.21044 100.81294 3000 450
  wp 20.33888 100.85637 3000 450
  objective survive

unit s8ef
  module f15c
  team hostile
  spawn 21.49484 101.24893 6000 197.6 480     # 150 km beyond Talbot: the merge is AFTER the release
  set gear up
  set task intercept
  set brief_gci 197 150 5000
  set store 1 aim120
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 4 aim120
  set brief_master_arm arm
  wp 19.61106 100.61071 6000 480
  objective survive

unit s8ful
  module mig29
  team hostile
  spawn 21.48397 101.28574 6000 197.6 450     # 4 km abeam the Eurofighter stand-in
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_mode rad
  set n019_emission illum
  set rwr on
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 7 r27r
  set store 5 r73
  set store 6 r73
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 19.61106 100.61071 6000 450
  objective survive

unit s8flg
  module mig23
  team hostile
  spawn 21.50570 101.21212 6000 197.6 450     # 4 km the other side
  set gear up
  set task intercept
  set brief_gci 197 150 5000
  set store 1 r24r
  set store 2 r24r
  set brief_master_arm arm
  wp 19.61106 100.61071 6000 450
  objective survive

unit s8cmd
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 20.21044 100.81294 ground 17.6 0      # Objective Talbot, the command centre

unit s8sa2
  module sa2
  team hostile
  spawn 20.09057 100.77243 ground 17.6 0      # 14 km short of the command centre, ON the run-in
  set alert ready
  set emcon free

unit s8sa9
  module sa18
  team hostile
  spawn 20.20909 100.81750 ground 17.6 0      # 500 m from the command centre: the point defence
  set alert ready
